@startuml
participant web: TripWebsite
box "Order Processing Center"
participant po: PurchaseOrderService
participant wf: WorkflowManager
participant cb: SupplierCallbackService
participant order: TripOrder
end box
participant notifications: Notifications
box "Other organizations" <<external>>
participant bank: Bank
participant supplier[i]: SupplierProvider
end box
web -> po: submit(tripOrder)
activate po
create order
po --> order: «create»
po ->> wf: orders.received
po --> web: orderId
deactivate po
activate wf
wf -> bank: capture(cardToken, amount)
activate bank
bank --> wf: captureId
deactivate bank
loop [for each supplier order]
wf -> supplier[i]: place(supplierOrder)
activate supplier[i]
supplier[i] --> wf: accepted
deactivate supplier[i]
end
wf -> order: mark_processing()
deactivate wf
loop [for each supplier answer]
supplier[i] -> cb: answer(supplierOrderId, decision)
activate cb
cb ->> wf: supplier.answered
cb --> supplier[i]: received
deactivate cb
activate wf
alt [decision is reject]
wf -> order: mark_failed()
wf ->> notifications: trip.failed
else [every supplier order confirmed]
wf -> order: mark_confirmed()
wf ->> notifications: trip.confirmed
end
deactivate wf
end
note right of web
Key: UML 2.5.1 sequence diagram.
Filled arrowhead: synchronous call.
Open arrowhead: asynchronous message.
Dashed arrow: reply or creation.
end note
note right of wf
wf hands orders.received to the payment
and supplier-order tasks
(services/opc/workflow.py:25) and
supplier.answered to the invoice task
(services/opc/workflow.py:29).
orders.received and supplier.answered
are work queues in the message broker
(deploy/broker.toml:8,
deploy/broker.toml:11).
A place() that cannot reach the supplier
is sent again every 60 s
(services/opc/supplier_task.py:10).
An answer changes the trip order only
while it is processing
(services/opc/invoice_task.py:33).
end note
@enduml
